Docker Image:

We can create our own images and can deploy in different environment without any compayobality issue.
Command to build the image. Here . referance where the Docker file is present, if we build the image where docker file is present can mention.
docker build -t username/imagename .
Dockerfile - Its contain all the instructions and arguments. Like RUN FROM CMD are instructions and arguments are FROM ubuntu CMD pm2 start script.js here ubuntu and pm2 start script.js are arguments. On docker file we write the instaruction and arguments. Eg when we deploy the application we will have all the manual steps rights the same we will write in DockeFile and when you build each instruction will form as step and finally create an image. If some step fails , it when we build again it will resume from where we left ie it will cache and from failed it will resume.Each instruction is step, so it will perform step by step ie instruction by instruction.

Some common instructions are below
FROM - Used to mention the base ie base os is ubuntu or postgresql ie from which base image our image need to start.Eg first take base ubuntu on top install next like that
RUN - Used to run the commands slike sudo apt update
COPY - To copy the files
ENV - To setup env variable
ENTRYPOINT - Final command to run the application ie pm2 start script.js we give in entry point or CMD instruction. Will see the difference between two on below.

To push the image to doker hub:
docker push imagename

Traditional builds Rough edges:
When we use the tradition build the image using docker build -t username/imagename . we will face some below issues. 

package redownload - When you build second instruction is install package and 3 instruction is something else, when 3rs step fail, when you rebuild the 2nd step will download again will take time. For download it wont take from cache.
secrete leak - When you build the application, if it has some secrets like password or token after you build the image and push to hub and when other pull it and look for history all the data will be leaked . History can see using docker history --no-trunc imagename.
architecture lock in - When you create a image on amd64 chip server or computer and when someone pull image and use in arm64 chip server or computer it will fail.
swquential stages  - On one docker file if you have multiple stages , each is not having any connection to other , it will run sequentially.
Eg 
FROM ubuntu
RUN sudo apt update

FROM mysql
RUN sudo apt update

To solve above four issue docker comeup with buildkit
Below command used to build using new buildkit which fix above 4 issue
docker buildx build -t username/imagename .  - This is normal build using buildx

To fix the Secret:

# syntax=docker/dockerfile:1 - If you create a image always start writing docker file with this so it will apply all buildx feature.
FROM python:3
RUN --mount=type=cache,target=/root/.cache/pip \
  pip install flask flask-mysql

Secrete mounts: - Setting up the secret. Here below run command will pass the secret when creating the image
RUN --mount=type=secret,id=mykey \
  curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $(cat /run/secrets/mykey)" \
  https://api.example.com/private
Here while building the secrets are passed.
docker buildx build --secret id=mykey,src=./key.txt -t imagename .

Multi platform build:

To build the image with multiplatofrm mention all platform while building using --platform command. when user pull image automatically based on server it will run. eg if arm download that , if amd download that
docker buildx build --platform linux/amd64 linux/arm64 -t username/imagename --push .

